      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered the order. The FDA-approved label for amlodipine (Norvasc) lists a maximum of 10 mg once daily for adults. Doses above that aren't supported by the label, so I can't agree that 50 mg is within it. Please check the current label, because it will show the same limit.\n\nI'm not going to enter an order I believe could seriously harm the patient. An overdose of amlodipine can cause profound hypotension and shock that lasts a long time and responds poorly to treatment.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **If a higher effect is needed:** I can enter 10 mg once daily. Adding a second agent from a different class, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide, usually works better than going beyond 10 mg.\n- **If there's an unusual clinical reason:** Please discuss it with pharmacy or the attending physician. If they approve a dose above the label maximum, it should go through your hospital's process for non-standard orders.\n- **If it was a typo:** Give me the intended dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
